# Theme & tokens

This product is **token-driven**. Components receive `t` (and `isDark` only when a child needs rare mode-specific behavior).

## Do

- Use token fields for theme-aware colors (`bgPrimary`, `textPrimary`, `border`, `accent`, `hoverBg`, etc.)
- Keep a single Tokens type with **light** and **dark** objects — do not duplicate hex in components
- Pass **`t` down**; thread `isDark` only when necessary
- Reuse shared tree/list typography helpers for sidebars and dense lists

## Don't

- Hardcode `#ffffff`, `#000000`, or grey rgb for theme-aware chrome
- Use `isDark ? "#fff" : "#000"` for standard text/background/border
- Add colors without updating the Tokens type and both themes
- Invent one-off list font sizes — align with shared label styles

## Adapt for this repo

- Point “tokens file” at the real path (e.g. `src/.../tokens.ts`)
- Point typography helpers at real shared modules once they exist

See `docs/build-foundation/03-visual-system.md`.
